摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DeepSeek Harness (dsh) container image: universal dev-container base, dsh auto-update on boot, compose + Quadlet examples","id":"gh:1333316853","install_available":false,"language":"Shell","name":"dsh-container","slug":"NIyueeE/dsh-container","topics":["deepseek-harness","docker","docker-compose","dsh","dsh-plugin","podman","podman-compose","quadlet"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness (dsh) container image: universal dev-container base, dsh auto-update on boot, compo"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"se + Quadlet examples"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh Container Image"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**DeepSeek Harness (`dsh`) as a batteries-included\ncontainer: agent, full toolchain, and reverse pro"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"xy in one image, built from the official source tags.**"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"### Docker Compose (Linux)"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"### Podman Quadlet (Linux, recommended)"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Both examples publish `127.0.0.1:3081` and mount one volume at `/home/dsh`. The user layer\n(`~/.dsh`"},{"id":"p10s2","text":", caches, user-installed tools) survives image upgrades; the system layer comes from\nthe image. The "},{"id":"p10s3","text":"first visit is redirected to dsh's launch token, and the browser keeps the session\ncookie from then "},{"id":"p10s4","text":"on, so there is no separate login form."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## What's inside"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"| Component | Description |"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"| Base image | `debian:13-slim` (moving tag; pass `BASE_IMAGE` to pin a digest) |\n| Toolchain | Node"},{"id":"p13s2","text":".js 24 LTS, pnpm, uv, Rust/cargo (+ rustfmt/clippy), git + git-lfs, build-essential + musl-tools, Ca"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"ddy, podman + crun, gh, yq. These are image-owned real binaries and upgrade with the image |\n| Agent"},{"id":"p13s4","text":" CLI tools | ripgrep, fd, python3, zip, openssh-client, tmux, sqlite3, vim.tiny/nano, less, rsync, w"},{"id":"p13s5","text":"get, tree, htop, tzdata, patch, plus a diagnostics set (dig/nc/socat/traceroute/iperf3/nft, file, nc"},{"id":"p13s6","text":"du, strace, zstd/lz4, bc, moreutils, pv, uuid-runtime), xdg-user-dirs (UI default workspace) and dev"},{"id":"p13s7","text":" tooling (just, shellcheck). All of them are baked into the system layer, so a fresh container never"},{"id":"p13s8","text":" re-downloads them (a runtime `apt install` would be lost on recreation) |\n| Nested containers | pod"},{"id":"p13s9","text":"man in-container (rootless) with `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR`, subuid/subgid and the network/sysctl defaults pr"},{"id":"p13s10","text":"econfigured; the host runtime must allow unprivileged user namespaces + `/dev/fuse` + `/dev/net/tun`"},{"id":"p13s11","text":" and must not mask the container's `/proc` (`--security-opt unmask=ALL`, Quadlet `Unmask=ALL`, Docke"},{"id":"p13s12","text":"r `systempaths=unconfined`); resource limits (`--memory`/`--cpus`) inside nested containers are not "},{"id":"p13s13","text":"enforced (cgroup v2 constraint); see docs/deployment.md § In-container podman |\n| dsh | Built from t"},{"id":"p13s14","text":"he official source tag into `/opt/deepseek-harness` (`DSH_TAG` pinnable; `latest` builds the newest "},{"id":"p13s15","text":"upstream tag, the only one the smoke gate verifies); no runtime auto-update |\n| Exposure | Caddy rev"},{"id":"p13s16","text":"erse proxy (`0.0.0.0:3081` → dsh's `127.0.0.1:3080`); preserves the browser `Host`/`Origin`, redirec"},{"id":"p13s17","text":"ts the first visit to dsh's login token, and keeps optional basic auth |\n| Supervisor | `dsh web` au"},{"id":"p13s18","text":"to-restarts on exit; `docker exec dsh dsh-restart` restarts it manually |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## Container-adapt plugin"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"All container-side adaptation of upstream dsh (0.2.1-alpha.3 and newer) lives in **one Cordis plugin"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"**,\nshipped with the image at `/opt/dsh-container-plugin` and mounted into the web profile via\n`dsh "},{"id":"p15s3","text":"ed with the image at `/opt/dsh-container-plugin` and mounted into the web profile via\n`dsh --patch`:"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"- **Launch-token redirect:** the plugin writes dsh's process launch token to\n`/tmp/dsh-caddy/launch-"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"token`; Caddy 302s a browser without a session cookie to `/?token=...`, and\ndsh sets an `HttpOnly; S"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"ameSite=Strict` cookie. The container never injects or rewrites the\nsession; the browser holds it.\n-"},{"id":"p16s4","text":" **Hidden settings-document button:** \"Open config file\" has no headless fallback upstream and\nwould"},{"id":"p16s5","text":" spawn `xdg-open` into nothing in a container. The plugin makes `settings/describe`\nreport `hasDocum"},{"id":"p16s6","text":"ent: false`, so the button never renders (upstream's own UI logic). Settings\npersist on the mounted "},{"id":"p16s7","text":"volume under `~/.dsh` (upstream v0.1.7+ keeps them per profile in\n`~/.dsh/profiles/<profile>/cordis."},{"id":"p16s8","text":"patch.yml`; the legacy `settings.yaml` is imported once).\n- **Plugins page card:** a small client ha"},{"id":"p16s9","text":"lf registers a built-in `plugins.item` card (no\nenable/disable switch) with a one-line summary and a"},{"id":"p16s10","text":" detail page describing the plugin and linking\nthe project repository.\n- **Payload post-processing:*"},{"id":"p16s11","text":"* three build-time steps run after `pnpm run build:official`. Images\ninlined at ≥ 100 KiB are extrac"},{"id":"p16s12","text":"ted to `/container-assets/<content-hash>` (served `immutable` by\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## Networking & security"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"- **Port model:** `dsh web` listens on `127.0.0.1:3080` (upstream rejects `--host 0.0.0.0`); the\nexp"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"osed port is `3081`, published on host loopback by the examples.\n- **The proxy preserves the fence:*"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"* Caddy forwards the browser `Host`/`Origin` unchanged, and dsh's\n`/api` fence is real. External aut"},{"id":"p18s4","text":"horities must be listed in `DSH_TRUSTED_HOST` (or derived from\n`DSH_PUBLIC_URL`); Caddy rejects any "},{"id":"p18s5","text":"other Host with 403, which is what stops DNS rebinding.\nAnyone who can reach `3081` can log in, so e"},{"id":"p18s6","text":"nable basic auth (`DSH_PROXY_USER`/`DSH_PROXY_PASSWORD`,\nset together or the supervisor refuses to s"},{"id":"p18s7","text":"tart) and keep the port firewalled. The\n`/api/remote.mux` WebSocket is exempt from basic auth (brows"},{"id":"p18s8","text":"ers do not reliably attach\n`Authorization` to upgrades) and is authenticated by the browser's `SameS"},{"id":"p18s9","text":"ite=Strict` cookie.\n- **Session held by the browser:** the first visit without a cookie is 302'd to "},{"id":"p18s10","text":"dsh's launch token;\ndsh sets the session cookie and the browser sends it back. There is no server-si"},{"id":"p18s11","text":"de cookie\ninjection. DeepSeek account sign-in still requires a loopback browser origin (an SSH tunne"},{"id":"p18s12","text":"l)\nrather than a public hostname; see docs/deployment.md § DeepSeek account sign-in.\n- **Streams, pa"},{"id":"p18s13","text":"yload and caching:** SSE/WebSocket pass through unbuffered (verified against Caddy\n2.6) and dsh's 2 "},{"id":"p18s14","text":"s heartbeat survives the hop. The client bundles are post-processed at build\ntime, so a cold page lo"},{"id":"p18s15","text":"ad measured in a headless browser is **≈1.6 MiB on the wire** against\n≈5.8 MiB for upstream's unproc"},{"id":"p18s16","text":"essed payload. The combined client-plugin bundle drops from 5.06 MiB\nto ≈1.0 MiB gzip, because image"},{"id":"p18s17","text":"s inlined at ≥ 100 KiB are extracted and fetched only when their\nscreen opens, and the bundles are m"},{"id":"p18s18","text":"inified. The index is `no-store` while the content-hashed\n`/assets/*` tree is served `immutable`, so"},{"id":"p18s19","text":" repeat visits are cheap.\n- **Telemetry off by default:** the entrypoint sets `DSH_TELEMETRY_MODE=DI"},{"id":"p18s20","text":"SABLED`, so the OTel\nfeedback uploader never sends anything unless you opt back in. Separately, upst"},{"id":"p18s21","text":"ream's\nDeepSeek session-log contributor is **on by default** and attaches session-log suffixes to\n[该"},{"id":"p18s22","text":"\nDeepSeek session-log contributor is **on by default** and attaches session-log suffixes to\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
